{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Inside her.</b> She examined her innards and said: Is it possible that these womb-parts would bear a child? These breasts that have dried up — would they draw milk? A comfort to her:" "<b>After the manner of women.</b> Suppleness of flesh. And the language of Mishnah (Middah 2:5): one who rubs the hair and moistens the flesh. Another interpretation: a term of עִדָּן; the time of the menstrual period."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:13.427820753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}